{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNXv5GqYgpJVyKm9MzNU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014UfP4CZBKu83tUtVznfg4L","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/proposal.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"; recorded only, not enforced yet\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,\"; enforced at the claim gate with the dollar caps\")\na=\"Tokens are also recorded per role (`tokens_per_day`, optionally per role; unset means no token cap; nothing is enforced yet). Counted tokens\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,\"Tokens are capped too (`tokens_per_day`, optionally per role; unset means no token cap), so a role on a model with no dollar price is capped by tokens alone. With U the tokens counted today, C the cap and W the role's largest reported job total, a candidate is refused when `U >= C` or `C - U < min(W, C)`: a role stops when what is left could not cover its worst job. Running jobs reserve nothing, and deterministic scanners are never checked. A job must pass both the dollar and the token check. If the token state cannot be read, the gate refuses with `budget state unreadable` and logs WARN `budget.read_failed`; a block is logged once a day as `budget.blocked`. The `budget` loop also posts one comment per token cap and UTC day, marked `<!-- ard:budget cap=tokens role=<kind>/<name> day=<YYYY-MM-DD> -->`, with numbers only. Counted tokens\")\na=\"The Reaper keeps running while the controller is paused.\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,a+\" The claim gate checks daily token caps as well as dollar caps (see Budgets); a running job is never killed for either cap, only new claims are refused.\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nmake test 2>&1 | tail -15; git -c core.excludesFile=/dev/null status --porcelain --untracked-files=all"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":173