{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNYG27tW79vvRYjuj6L5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The token check is now part of the claim gate, so a job has to pass both the dollar check and the token check. `make test` passes, `go vet ./internal/...` is clean, and the changed files are gofmt-clean.\n\n- **Rule:** with U tokens used today, cap C and worst job W, a role is refused when `U >= C` or `C - U < min(W, C)`. Running jobs reserve nothing, and deterministic scanners are never checked.\n- **Unreadable state:** the gate refuses with `budget state unreadable` and logs a WARN `budget.read_failed`.\n- **Logging:** the first block per role per UTC day logs `budget.blocked`.\n- **Notice:** the status issue gets one comment per token cap per UTC day, with the marker from the issue. Repeats are suppressed through the existing `budget_capped` event, so a restart doesn't repost. The dollar notice is unchanged.\n- **Report:** `TokenReport` (all capped roles) and `TokenCapped` (blocked ones only) are in `internal/budget/tokens.go`.\n- **Wiring:** `internal/servecmd/budget.go` hooks the store in as the token reader. `internal/pool/pool.go` changed comments only.\n- **Docs:** `docs/proposal.md` has the Budgets, Configuration and Executors/Reaper text.\n- **Tests:** a new `internal/budget/tokens_test.go` covers each \"Done when\" item from the issue: the rule table, a role capped by tokens with no dollar figure, both caps, the 00:00 UTC reset on a fake clock, and one comment per cap per day.\n\nA maintainer should still review the claim rule and the fail-closed path, as the issue asks. The token notice marker has a different format from the existing dollar one; I kept both.\n\nThe report is written to `.ard/242/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":865,"cache_read_input_tokens":42488,"cache_